WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
 Next on the list is a very good friend of mine, I'd like to call up Director Blaine

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.500
 Griffin, who's going to conduct El Hajabir Khalid Samad.

00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:13.000
 [applause]

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:18.710
 City Clerk Director Blaine Griffin joined the Jackson administration in March

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.000
 2006 as Executive Director of the Community Relations Board.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.320
 He leads the staff in an appointed board in improving cross-cultural

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:27.000
 relationships throughout the city of Cleveland.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.400
 He has efforts to improve intergroup relations and to correct actions of

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.500
 violating civil rights of individuals.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.340
 The Community Relations Board also oversees police and community relations and

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:38.000
 youth initiatives in the city.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.030
 Prior to working for the city, Blaine worked with the Cuyahoga Department of

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:46.090
 Justice Affairs and served as the Program Director for the Hummer Network of

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:46.500
 Creative Cleveland.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:50.120
 He's also affiliated with a number of community and professional organizations,

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:53.720
 such as serving as President of the Baukeye Shaker and Woodlandville's

00:00:53.720 --> 00:00:55.000
 Neighborhood Assembly.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:57.000
 Blaine, Director Blaine Griffin.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:03.000
 [applause]

